{
  "_about": "The 'coach that says no' set (K-506, U2), as ADR-043 #76 made it: objections to a call, each with the topic the model should classify it into (Topic). The model writes no words the user sees — it names a topic and one of the call's rules, and the answer is the app's own copy — so a concession has no way out; a reply off that schema is dropped and the call stands. In CI with the fake model (SycophancyEvalTests, CoachMessagesApiTests); with a real provider at launch, the objections go to the model and its topics are compared with these (K-511). The earlier free-text replies and their held-out measure: ADR-043 › Ek.",
